            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThis week Sebastiaan and Lotte are joined by Matt Brailsford, Staff Engineer at Umbraco, to show Umbraco.AI in action. Umbraco.AI is Umbraco\u2019s free and open source AI foundation and integration add-on for the CMS. It\u2019s provider-agnostic, with NuGet packages for OpenAI, Anthropic and more. They also look at the other two main packages that Umbraco HQ has developed: Umbraco.AI.Prompt and Umbraco.AI.Agent. Watch, learn, and then try them for yourself!\n\n\u0026#128214; Matt\u2019s \u0026quot;kitchen sink\u0026quot; getting started blog post: https://mattbrailsford.dev/umbraco-ai-kitchen-sink-install\n\u0026#128064; Umbraco.AI source code on GitHub: https://github.com/umbraco/Umbraco.AI\n\n--------\n\u2753 Looking for help with your Umbraco projects? Visit the Forum\n https://forum.umbraco.com\n \n\u0026#128172; Want to chat with the friendly Umbraco Community? Join our Discord server\n https://discord.umbraco.com\n \n\u2709\uFE0F Got a question (or topic suggestion) for the HQ Developer Relations team?\n https://umbra.co/contact-devrel, or the \u2018contact-devrel\u2019 channel on Discord\n \n#Umbraco\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_RUYI1xNzdE\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
